The attached image illustrates the physical characterization of Nano-11 nanoparticles. The left panel displays a Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image, revealing spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like appearance, confirming their dendrimer-like alpha-D-glucan structure. The right panel presents a particle size distribution histogram, indicating a Z-average hydrodynamic diameter for Nano-11 predominantly ranging from 30 to 110 nm, with a peak around 70-80 nm. These morphological and size attributes are critical for the nanoparticles' efficient uptake by dendritic cells and their role as an effective vaccine adjuvant.